computing/prologue/asy/tm_exercises

Files here show the history of computations with a Turing machine.  To
ensure that they are right, we use the Turing machine emulator
  computing/src/scheme/prologue/turing-machine.rkt
which gives output that shows a sequence of machine configurations in
ASCII. 
Those generated files are placed into tmp/*.out.

We convert that outputs from .out files to .asy files using the
Python script in computing/bin/turing_machine.  This directory's
Makefile runs that script to give the output .asy files, and then
runs Asymptote to generate the .pdf's that the book needs.
The .asy and .pdf files are placed into the pdfs/ directory.
Most of the outputs are for exercises but a few are for the
text body.

In short, use the command `make'.
